        "original_id": "7f60ddea-e13b-5f5d-bd21-13256b07e532",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Kniphofia, Baptisia\n- Plant taxonomy: genera, family Asphodelaceae\n- Plant characteristics: flowering, herbaceous perennials, pea-like flowers, pods\n\nFacts:\n- Kniphofia is a genus of flowering plants in the family Asphodelaceae that was first described as a genus in 1794.\n- Kniphofia is also called tritoma, red hot poker, torch lily, knofflers, or poker plant.\n- Baptisia plants are flowering herbaceous perennials.\n- Baptisia plants have pea-like flowers followed by pods that are sometimes inflated.",
